            <ArticleTitle>Revision peripheral nerve surgery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>305-18</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The treatment of chronic neuropathic pain with revision surgical procedures can be beneficial. A thorough evaluation can help to guide treatment to optimize outcome. With an increasing understanding of the pain-generating mechanisms and the appropriate application of surgical interventions, quality of life and function continues to be improved in patients who have otherwise significant disability.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
